@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.12.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.12.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.12.0 (2026-11-24): Chapter 11 code story done. A finding to the Owner, not repaired here: the property names that this and earlier lineage files in the repository use for objectives, metrics, observations, the backlog members and scope deliverables (for example observedValue, hasMetric, hasBacklogMember, hasScopeDeliverable) are not defined in the BRSF T-Box 1.181.0, which names other ones (for example pursuesObjective, scopeRealizesObjective); the register check does not look for them. This file follows the repository's existing practice."""@en .

ex:TK11_Code_11_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "03-materials/ch11/source/ch11_code_source_v1_0_0.json holds the 19 chapter 11 examples once: 10 traced to a block of the book (copy, copytree, move, dry run, listing, walk, mkdir, ZIP write, extract, the finished backup program) and 9 with a named reason in their own book field (the slide teaches it, the book has no code block for it; written in the book's style, 4 to 6 lines). Interpreter prompts removed (Owner's option C), results are print lines. Sample files are hidden setup lines in a temporary folder. Two small changes to keep the same output on every machine: folders and files are sorted in the walk and in the listing. Code lines fell from 285 to 113; 49 percent of them equal a book line, against 7 percent before." .
ex:TK11_Code_11_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Log 08-tooling/code-source/logs_v1_0_0/ch11_source_outputs.log: each of the 19 examples runs to the end and gives the same output twice; the backup program prints exactly the four lines the book shows (Creating spam_1.zip, Adding files in folder spam, Adding file file1.txt, Done); the ZIP example gives the book's sizes 50000 and 97. Code check C1 and C4 pass on the source and its examples list. Run by the agent that wrote the examples, so not independent. Open and named: the deck and page conditions (C2, C3) belong to the next stories; the Owner's reading of the examples is the criterion that no tool can run. Results show PosixPath where the book shows WindowsPath, as the machine here is not Windows." .
ex:ST11_Code_11 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met; see its tasks. The strict wording of the objective (traced to a block of the book) is met by 10 of 19; the other 9 have a named reason, as the Definition of Done allows. This is reported to the Owner at closure." .
ex:Obs1_Obj11_TracedExamples a backlog:MetricObservation ; backlog:observationForMetric ex:Metric_Obj11_TracedExamples ; backlog:observedValue 10 ; backlog:observedAt "2026-11-24T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:comment "Chapter 11 only: 10 of 19 examples traced to a book code block, 9 more with a named reason (113 code lines, 49 percent equal to a book line). Chapter 10 not yet done." .
ex:DoD11_TracedCode rdfs:comment "Run on 2026-11-24 for chapter 11: 10 traced, 9 with a named reason, none without either. Chapter 10 still to run; the status stays NotYetEnforceable (one value only) until it has run for both chapters, then it is set once." .
